{"kind":"request","text":"Conservative Tailapp upgrades: design note first, then implementation of provenance, classification, upgrade plan, --apply-safe, backups, and explicit continue/reset","body":{"conditions":"PROVENANCE: operator direction, hugh, 2026-08-31 (gap closure for #2273 per checker audit: nothing of this request has been delivered - promise eae15208 was repurposed to the Copilot mapping). This is a design-first item. STAGE A (deliver first, docs-only, review to checker): a design note under notes/ resolving how to meet every #2273 condition: durable provenance per first-party bundle installation (built-in origin, bundle name, installed release/baseline source digest, comparison basis - where it is stored and how it survives continue/reset); a machine-readable upgrade plan classifying every app as user-generated, pristine built-in, or modified built-in, reporting runtime compatibility separately; the rule that generated and modified apps are never rewritten, merged, activated, or reset automatically, with a three-way upstream/current/baseline diff or conflict report for modified built-ins; --apply-safe semantics limited to pristine built-ins whose release metadata certifies continuation safety, after validation and optimistic-revision checks; explicit app selection and confirmation for reset-requiring or non-certified changes, never inferring safety from schema shape; a mandatory user-selected backup location with capacity/error handling and a documented restore path before any reset or nontrivial change; explicit continue/reset commands; draft protection; the test matrix for every classification and failed/rollback path; and the statement that normal binary upgrades leave custom apps and data untouched. The note must also reconcile with the existing manual procedure in cli.md (Upgrading an existing resident) and the recent live restore. STAGE B (after the note is approved): implementation in reviewable stages. GATES per stage: full battery, demo; per-file full-SHA artifacts; review to checker against the #2273 conditions verbatim.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}